WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.799
The bloopers from the Avengers films might
be some of the funniest we've seen in a while.

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:08.700
In fact, they're so funny that it's hard not
to fall in love with the films all over again.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.700
Not so tough props

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.379
In the realm of superheroes, especially Norse
mythology-derived superheroes, you're only

00:00:14.379 --> 00:00:15.730
as good as your accessories.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:21.930
Thor has quite a few: his long red cape, his
long blond hair, and his mighty hammer Mjolnir.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.410
When it comes to his hammer, it's so tough
and unbreakable that it took the might of

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.400
Hela, the goddess of death, to finally break
it in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.740
Maybe they got the idea for that moment from
this blooper in which Thor's magical hammer

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.340
sure seems like a very breakable prop.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:50.620
One of the few things as iconic as Thor's
hammer in the MCU is Captain America's shield.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.350
It's about as classic as superhero equipment
gets and it's so powerful that Cap routinely

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.760
busts through walls and locks with it.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.260
Unfortunately, the real prop shield they use
in the filming is a lot less useful than its

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.240
fictional counterpart.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:08.580
Vocal flubs

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:12.730
It's easy for the comic book version of Bruce
Banner to just rattle off scientific terms

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.490
because someone can just scribble them into
a speech bubble.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:20.050
It's clearly a bit harder for actors to say
all those complicated words in real life.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:24.280
Just watch Mark Ruffalo as he struggles to
deliver what's clearly a mouthful of technical

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.160
mumbo-jumbo in The Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.740
In a deleted scene in Iron Man 3, Trevor Slattery
successfully passes himself off as a Russian

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:46.060
over the phone, which leads to Colonel James
Rhodes asking him to try out a number of other

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.060
voices.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.570
It's really just a chance for Academy Award-winning
actor Sir Ben Kingsley to display his acting

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:55.930
ability and dialect talent — because he
can handle every suggestion actor Don Cheadle

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.150
throws his way.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.150
“Jamaican”

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.350
“I come from Jamaica.”

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:01.030
“Can you do French?”

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.720
“Allo, je suis Francais.”

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.350
“Can you do like, a Spanish.”

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.980
“I can do, but…”

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.120
“Shut up!’

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.300
Well, almost every suggestion.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.740
“Can you do British?"

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:12.900
"Well, I am British."

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:13.720
Hulk run away!

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:19.540
When Bruce Banner turns into the Hulk to punch
a giant alien in The Avengers, it's a stand-up-and-clap

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:20.540
moment.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.500
However, as it turns out, that wasn't exactly
the first instinct that actor Mark Ruffalo

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.040
had when facing down a CGI monstrosity.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.560
“Dudes, you’re on your own!”

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.890
Considering how terrifying the aliens looked
on the big screen, it's hard to fault Ruffalo's

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:42.890
acting instincts.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.890
Short-circuiting Vision

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:48.270
Paul Bettany used to just provide the voice
of JARVIS in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.320
but these days he's using his whole self to
play Vision.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.569
Bettany is barely recognizable under all that
red makeup.

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:59.470
While he certainly looks the part of the super-advanced
robot, he's acting more like a malfunctioning

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:02.640
computer in this blooper from Captain America:
Civil War:

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.920
Not so serious

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:15.270
One of the most impressive things about the
MCU is that the actors are able to take it

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.849
all seriously when surrounded by goofy costumes
and CGI monsters.

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:23.819
It's the kind of true commitment to character
that explains why they get paid so much.

00:03:23.819 --> 00:03:28.160
However, that doesn't mean there aren't a
few moments where that seriousness cuts out.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.670
In this lineup of stern, determined-looking
heroes for Avengers: Infinity War, Benedict

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.660
Wong just couldn't keep the steely resolve
on his face for more than a few seconds.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:47.480
Captain America's hot tip

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:52.050
Spider-Man: Homecoming included one of the
most memorable cameos in MCU history when

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:58.300
Chris Evans' Captain America pops in via green-screened
video to deliver some corny, educational advice

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.560
to the students of Peter's high school.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.460
"So.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.560
You got detention.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.640
You screwed up."

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.550
However, one particular video is just a bit
too over the top for Evans to make it through

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:13.750
without cracking up.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.510
"Hi, I'm Captain America.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:20.169
Whether you're a student or a soldier, there's
one thing that will always give you an edge:

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:21.400
A hot lunch."

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:23.860
Room to vroom

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.029
Ant-Man and the Wasp was packed with plenty
of car chases through San Francisco, a city

00:04:28.029 --> 00:04:31.330
full of steep hills, big curves, and tons
of traffic.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:36.069
In this blooper, Paul Rudd gets into character
as he prepares to shoot one of those sequences:

00:04:36.069 --> 00:04:37.760
“Good scene, everyone, let’s have lunch.”

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.540
“Best scene in the movie!”

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.419
“Is it bad if I start saying this, ‘Vroom
vroom, vroom vroom vroom!’”

00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:46.419
Stan the Man

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:50.590
An MCU movie made in the last few years just
wouldn't be complete without a Stan Lee appearance,

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:54.620
and Ant-Man and the Wasp had one of the legendary
creator's best cameos.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:59.139
As Scott Lang, Hope Van Dyne, and their associates
battle bad guys through the twisty streets

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:05.099
of San Francisco, Lee shows up as a guy whose
car gets shrunk by Ant-Man's signature technology:

00:05:05.099 --> 00:05:11.460
"Well, the '60s were fun, but now I'm paying
for it."

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:16.129
It turns out that's just the take filmmakers
decided on; they had Lee go through a huge

00:05:16.129 --> 00:05:17.870
list of funny possibilities.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.860
"Aw no, my sandwich was in there!"

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.300
"Well, at least now I'll be able to park in
San Francisco."

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.300
Great job, Heidecker!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:30.949
The two Ant-Man movies are pretty much the
funniest of all the MCU standalone flicks.

00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:35.400
The casts of both feature performers with
a knack for comedy, including Walton Goggins,

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.219
Michael Peña, Randall Park, and Judy Greer.

00:05:38.219 --> 00:05:42.720
Even so, it's a pleasant surprise for viewers
to suddenly encounter Tim Heidecker, a comedy

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:47.610
innovator known for his bizarre, boundary-pushing
work on cult TV favorites like Tim and Eric

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.330
Awesome Show, Great Job!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.819
In Ant-Man and the Wasp, he plays the leader
of a San Francisco Bay boat tour guide.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:57.559
Some of Heidecker's best lines were unfortunately
left for the blooper reel though.

00:05:57.559 --> 00:05:58.800
“I freak for whales.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.379
I've loved them ever since I was a kid.

00:06:00.379 --> 00:06:04.029
I'm not trained really, or know anything about
biology.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:05.930
I've memorized some things, but I couldn't
go deep.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:06.930
Did you say Wakanda?

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.960
Black Panther is a crowning achievement in
filmmaking, and it also gave the world one

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.020
of the all-time great movie catchphrases.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.780
It even makes an appearance in Avengers: Infinity
War.:

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.700
"Wakanda forever!"

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:25.809
Since Black Panther's release in early 2018,
millions have flashed each other the crossed-arms

00:06:25.809 --> 00:06:26.809
salute.

00:06:26.809 --> 00:06:30.520
By now, everyone knows how to say "Wakanda"
correctly, but during the film's production,

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.530
a few cast members had trouble getting it
down.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:37.589
In this clip, neither Martin Freeman or Danai
Gurira are confident in their ability.

00:06:37.589 --> 00:06:41.020
“The thing that was on your arm?

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.080
Is from Wakanda?”

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.830
“Wakanda will neve ----BLEEP!”

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:46.830
Doctor of dance

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.149
Doctor Strange was a harder sell than your
typical superhero movie.

00:06:50.149 --> 00:06:54.189
After all, Doctor Stephen Strange's powers
come from an ability to connect with the worlds

00:06:54.189 --> 00:06:55.940
of mysticism and magic.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:07:00.159
To effectively ground that in reality, the
filmmakers required the services of actor

00:07:00.159 --> 00:07:05.610
with extensive classical training and an impressive
résumé full of award-winning dramatic roles.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:09.979
That actor: Benedict Cumberbatch, who earned
widespread acclaim for his work in Sherlock

00:07:09.979 --> 00:07:11.470
and The Imitation Game.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.939
But who knew that Cumberbatch could be so
silly?

00:07:13.939 --> 00:07:18.669
Underneath all the pomp and circumstance,
he's just as goofy on set as a wacky comic

00:07:18.669 --> 00:07:19.669
actor.

00:07:19.669 --> 00:07:23.990
Judging from this blooper reel, he's especially
down to get down, breaking into dance routines

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:25.660
while filming his scenes.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.860
It's apparently contagious, because most of
his co-stars got in on the dance craze, too.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:40.639
Asgard's funniest home videos

00:07:40.639 --> 00:07:44.369
One of television's longest-running hits is
America's Funniest Home Videos.

00:07:44.369 --> 00:07:50.309
Debuting in 1990, this long-running series
has delighted the masses with miles of poorly-shot

00:07:50.309 --> 00:07:53.810
and grainy footage of grown men getting hit
in the private parts.

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:58.979
The MCU movies, for all their big-budget set
pieces, aren't immune to that simple joy getting

00:07:58.979 --> 00:08:00.789
included on the blooper reel.

00:08:00.789 --> 00:08:01.820
"Did I hit your testicle?"

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.480
"I'm fine."

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.599
Comedy Gold(blum)

00:08:08.599 --> 00:08:13.339
In the '80s and '90s, Jeff Goldblum brought
a disarming charm and off-center sensibility

00:08:13.339 --> 00:08:17.969
to his roles in otherwise straightforward
movies like Jurassic Park and Independence

00:08:17.969 --> 00:08:18.969
Day.

00:08:18.969 --> 00:08:21.979
In doing so, he made them much better than
they otherwise could've been without him.

00:08:21.979 --> 00:08:26.599
It makes sense then that when director Taika
Waititi took the Thor movies in a cosmic and

00:08:26.599 --> 00:08:30.509
comedic direction with Thor: Ragnarok, he
brought Goldblum in for a role.

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:35.160
Goldblum plays the Grandmaster, the most hedonistic
of all the Elders of the Universe.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.680
The actor brings his trademark looseness and
an almost jazz-like approach to the movie,

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.650
which is noticeable even when he's goofing
off between takes.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.960
“Watch this.”

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.380
"Loki, take it away."

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:53.240
The cape can't cope

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:57.590
Thor's wardrobe is about as eye-catching as
the lightning that often accompanies the character.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:02.450
In addition to Chris Hemsworth's own indisputable
good looks, Thor usually rocks a tight metal

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:06.090
shirt, rad pants, and one undeniably great
cape.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:10.120
But while the accessory might be stylish,
it can be pretty temperamental.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:14.770
On the set of Thor: The Dark World, Hemsworth
tries his best to act, but he has trouble

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:16.640
due to an unpredictable co-star: His cape.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:27.600
Iron Man can't suit up

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.950
Science fiction films and superhero movies
are full of mythology, backstory, and their

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.470
own sets of rules.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:39.130
Iron Man 3 is a sci-fi film as well as a superhero
movie, and it's got a lot specific words and

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:44.610
jargon its actors need to clearly and slowly
deliver so the action around them makes sense.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:49.050
It's a delicate balance to nail the terminology
that's been part of a comic or cinematic universe

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:53.030
for years so it satisfies both hardcore and
new fans alike.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:57.740
That's why Marvel and its filmmakers hire
top-notch talent to deliver the written lines.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:02.160
Actors like Robert Downey Jr. have the training,
skill, and talent necessary to say all that

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.300
technical talk in a believable way.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:08.400
Still, sometimes it's hard to get those words
out, because even for an actor of Downey's

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.630
caliber, there's a lot to remember.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.750
In Iron Man 3, Tony Stark has to recall his
various super-suits.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:19.200
There are a lot of them, and in this blooper,
Downey Jr. needs the assistance of the Heartbreaker

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.550
armor to help out the armor whose… name
escapes him.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.120
"Heartbreaker, will you help… what's his
name?

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:26.620
Red snapper?"

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:27.120
Wild, wild goat

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:32.330
While the MCU movies enjoy a lot of cast overlap
for their various superheroic characters,

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:37.160
Black Panther came out of nowhere to introduce
many fantastic characters to the Marvel Cinematic

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.160
Universe.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:42.070
It also had the added benefit of making huge
stars out of the actors and actresses who

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.090
portrayed them.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:47.600
Chadwick Boseman had attained some fame after
playing Jackie Robinson and James Brown in

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:52.620
42 and Get On Up, respectively, while Lupita
Nyong'o achieved her breakthrough with 12

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:53.740
Years a Slave.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:58.460
Now they're A-listers thanks to their roles
at the top of the cast of this superhero action

00:10:58.460 --> 00:10:59.460
blockbuster.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:04.240
Danai Gurira established a big-screen career
for herself beyond her role as the katana-wielding

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:09.180
Michonne on The Walking Dead, but in this
blooper, she's quickly and effectively upstaged

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.080
by yet another breakout MCU star: a goat.

